WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:08.770
- [Mark] So, Stone.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:09.603
- [Stone] Yes, sir.

00:00:09.603 --> 00:00:10.436
- [Mark] Welcome back.

00:00:10.436 --> 00:00:11.667
- [Stone] Hey, what's going
on, Mark, how you doing?

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.260
- [Mark] What you got in your hand there?

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.600
- Hey, look here, man,

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.538
I seen this little item right here, man.

00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:19.063
It brought back some cold memories for me.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.253
Hands of Stone actually
was reactivating this.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.953
What I remember mostly about these,

00:00:27.953 --> 00:00:30.460
somebody owed my folks money,

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.850
and I've come through with the small ones.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.940
They used to have a
little Louisville Slugger,

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.660
they used to give it at the
opening day at Dodger's Stadium.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.240
It was wood about the same size,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.390
probably about the same,

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.560
probably a little smaller in this area.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.501
But what I used to like about it most,

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:49.425
is when you walk up, they can't see him.

00:00:49.425 --> 00:00:51.320
And then when you come
up, you pull it out.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.600
You don't have to hit him in
the face or nothing like that.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.070
It's about some money.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.310
So when you get at them,

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:02.310
you say bah, bah, them knees,
they automatically fall.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:03.809
And the cold part about that,

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:04.642
they going to remember that

00:01:04.642 --> 00:01:07.433
for about three, four months after that.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.250
It's a cold, cold thing,

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.610
but it'll get the message.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:16.400
So when somebody else see that
dude limping down the street

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.930
they'll be like, oh, he must
have owed such and such money.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.834
So it's like sending a message

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.900
to all the people that
the loan sharks are doing.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.300
That that's what's going to happen to you

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.820
if you don't pay me my money.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.076
And once we started doing that

00:01:29.076 --> 00:01:31.015
it didn't take a whole lot of people.

00:01:31.015 --> 00:01:33.236
After three or four people walk around,

00:01:33.236 --> 00:01:37.195
hobbling around people was
paying they money on time.

00:01:37.195 --> 00:01:40.710
Some people was even paying
it a couple of nights earlier.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.010
But one time, man

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.180
it was a little cat that
wanted to be, you know

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.480
he wanted to be a part of our little crew,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.630
what we was doing.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.143
'Cause we had separated ourselves

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.613
from everybody else that was hanging out,

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.540
and he was like, nah, man, I'm waiting.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.160
Put me on, put me on.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.033
I ended up,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.538
where I was from

00:02:02.538 --> 00:02:03.371
(indistinct) if we put that out there.

00:02:03.371 --> 00:02:05.670
But where I was from,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.759
I ended up making him my little homeboy.

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:10.860
And he started claiming my
neighborhood and everything.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:11.730
But the little dude, man,

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.090
he was probably about 19 years old, man.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.780
And he really wanted to hang out with us.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.420
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.477
And I'm like, alright, go let
him see, see what he can do.

00:02:21.477 --> 00:02:23.950
He wasn't no big old dude either.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.727
That's why I was tripping off of him.

00:02:25.727 --> 00:02:27.610
But the dude go.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.320
He was like, man, you
owe such such money, man.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.437
You supposed to be paying.

00:02:31.437 --> 00:02:33.280
And I'm like, you know,

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.850
I ain't saying that I'm
just looking at him.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.330
And he like man, you got the money?

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.760
And the boy was like,
man, I'm going to pay you,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.840
and he fired on him.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.750
And after he hit him,
my homie had the bat.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.850
He run, snatched the bat from him,

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.500
and just kicked up all
in the dude's head, man.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.790
I grabbed this little dude,
man, hold up man, hold up man.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.506
He's like, no, he's
going to pay that money.

00:02:58.506 --> 00:03:03.359
And he had zoned out so
bad that when he went out

00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:05.790
you couldn't even send him by himself.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.870
You know, sorry to say,

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.040
but this little kid
right now got life, man.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.565
But that's what he was doing, man.

00:03:11.565 --> 00:03:13.457
Any situation he was in

00:03:13.457 --> 00:03:16.167
I don't know what was
going in his head man,

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:17.994
but he is zoned out

00:03:17.994 --> 00:03:22.530
and it was all murder, death,
kill with him. For anything.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.090
And you know, I put him
on my turf, you know,

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:29.270
the homies loved him and all
that because he was an idiot.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.940
But you know, I really still
kind of feel kind of bad, man.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.460
I still write dude, time to time, man.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.721
You know, I ain't got no
whole bunch, but you know,

00:03:36.721 --> 00:03:39.049
probably once every
like three, four months

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:42.040
I might shoot him like 30, 40 bucks

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.610
get you a case of soups or something,

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.690
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.416
'Cause I remember him before
he turned into what he was.

00:03:47.416 --> 00:03:51.242
I mean, I ain't gonna go
all in no guilt with myself

00:03:51.242 --> 00:03:53.857
but you know, that's
what it was out there.

00:03:53.857 --> 00:03:54.943
You know?

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:59.400
I didn't seen him do some
stuff on his own where, I mean,

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.555
I don't know what I, I'm
trying to keep it where,

00:04:02.555 --> 00:04:04.146
you know, Dragnet say?

00:04:04.146 --> 00:04:06.603
Names are changed to protect the innocent.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.333
Yeah, man, I seen (indistinct)
set this tent on fire, man.

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:12.593
But folks was in there asleep, right.

00:04:13.861 --> 00:04:14.710
And we all, you know,

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:17.280
I think he was owing $100 or something

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.210
dude was supposed to owe.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.520
He was like, man, let me go get it.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.620
So they go and I guess
they in a cocaine coma

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.516
because he's banging on the
tent, banging on the tent,

00:04:28.516 --> 00:04:30.944
and don't nobody answer.

00:04:30.944 --> 00:04:34.410
He strike out and run down
the street, come back.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.638
He come back, banging on their tent again.

00:04:36.638 --> 00:04:38.565
Don't nobody know what he doing

00:04:38.565 --> 00:04:40.780
but he got some lighter fluid in his hand

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.270
and he knocking on the
tent, all around the tent,

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:46.090
but he's sprinkling a
lighter fluid on the tent.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.270
And he said, oh, you
ain't going to wake up?

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.990
He took a match and struck it.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.470
And poof.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.470
And it immediately, you
know, that's plastic

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:56.032
and immediately go up in flames, right?

00:04:56.032 --> 00:04:58.160
And it was a dude and a female in there,

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.200
and they woke up, and the tent,

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.550
I think went up and like
probably about 10, 15 seconds.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:06.394
Whole tent engulfed in flames.

00:05:06.394 --> 00:05:10.863
When they come running out,
the dude came out first.

00:05:10.863 --> 00:05:12.690
I don't know if you know anything

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.690
about that plastic on them
tents and the zippers.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.270
If it's on fire, you're not
going to find the zipper.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:22.719
So when he come running
out bam with the first one,

00:05:22.719 --> 00:05:26.060
he went out, the plastic,
stuck on him still.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.804
So when he ran out, he come out

00:05:27.804 --> 00:05:29.950
the front of him was all on fire.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:32.080
They have to rolled him on the ground.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.700
And a little dude still went

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.600
and tried to get the money from him.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.600
He was all in his pocket and everything.

00:05:40.182 --> 00:05:42.740
Yeah. I think about
some of that stuff, man,

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.770
and I thank God today,
man, I'm still here.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:46.603
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:46.603 --> 00:05:48.606
That's why today I do try and help folks.

00:05:48.606 --> 00:05:52.530
You know, I'm like, you know,
he ain't done with me yet.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.457
I still got my character faults, man.

00:05:54.457 --> 00:05:57.879
But I really think about
stuff before I do it today.

00:05:57.879 --> 00:06:01.674
And I think if what if that
was my cousin or my uncle.

00:06:01.674 --> 00:06:03.020
So that's why a lot

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.942
of stuff I don't get myself caught up in.

00:06:04.942 --> 00:06:07.124
You know, I'm still who I am.

00:06:07.124 --> 00:06:09.040
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.254
You know, I might even get drunk out here

00:06:11.254 --> 00:06:13.550
and say cuss a few times,

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:17.353
but for the most part,
man, I look at it, man ,

00:06:17.353 --> 00:06:19.820
I don't even see it work for
you, know what I'm saying?

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.506
I think I...

00:06:22.506 --> 00:06:25.056
Well I'm going to bring
you back a little bit, man.

00:06:27.414 --> 00:06:28.247
'82, '83

00:06:28.247 --> 00:06:32.460
we was really turned up
before I came out here.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:35.170
I think I came out here like '87, '88.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:38.270
A lot of my older homeboys had got life

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:41.977
and dudes just coming home now

00:06:41.977 --> 00:06:46.226
like '82, 1983, '84.

00:06:46.226 --> 00:06:49.730
The year I graduated was '84.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:54.730
So basically for the most
part of my, my era, I'm 53,

00:06:54.731 --> 00:06:56.230
Most of the kids,

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.670
'cause a lot of them got
life in my neighborhood.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:03.470
So like '84 to '88,

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:05.363
them dudes is just coming home now,

00:07:06.436 --> 00:07:07.638
whole life gone.

00:07:07.638 --> 00:07:12.330
They whole mentality,
everything is still prison.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:15.420
And you know, I did a few years in there.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.410
I didn't really do no long stretch.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.769
And I look at the way I think now

00:07:19.769 --> 00:07:22.675
and the way they think,

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:25.042
I mean I was well on my way to that,

00:07:25.042 --> 00:07:26.875
but wow, it's just crazy.

00:07:26.875 --> 00:07:31.807
Their whole, this right here,
is foreign to them really.

00:07:31.807 --> 00:07:34.450
They feel more at home in there,

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.990
be like, man, this just regular stuff.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.930
You know, I thank God every night, man,

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.638
that I didn't have to go through that.

00:07:43.638 --> 00:07:45.883
And I don't think I could do a day, bro.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:50.588
So for the most part I do
keep myself straight, man.

00:07:50.588 --> 00:07:52.620
- [Mark] You grew up in South central?

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:53.453
- [Rock] Yes I did.

00:07:53.453 --> 00:07:55.089
- [Mark] And what do you see the problem

00:07:55.089 --> 00:07:57.176
with like that community,

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:59.610
and so many families are broken.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.810
- [Rock] It's real easy.

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:03.819
For the most part,

00:08:03.819 --> 00:08:06.030
I'm gonna take it back to me, 53.

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:09.238
Uncles, aunties, everybody, like they say,

00:08:09.238 --> 00:08:11.543
it takes a village to raise a child.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:14.803
The drug epidemic came,

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:19.420
basically what when Oliver
North went over there,

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:23.260
with Noriega, with Bush CIA.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.093
Anyway--

00:08:24.093 --> 00:08:26.240
- [Mark] But crack hit
the black communities

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.500
really hard, right?

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:32.500
- [Rock] Our mentors and
roll models started off,

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.210
when I was young,

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:35.650
they was players,

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:38.440
it was a rich man high,

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.190
to smoke cocaine.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:42.713
So then, you know, everybody
wants to be players, boss,

00:08:42.713 --> 00:08:47.713
you know, as it progressed
cause you never baskets,

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.253
but none of that shit,
man, when I was young.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:54.110
But for the most part, all those dudes

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:56.714
they're the ones that
ended up getting rich

00:08:56.714 --> 00:09:01.270
are gone to jail for life became these

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.564
pushing baskets.

00:09:02.564 --> 00:09:03.897
And then a young kid,

00:09:03.897 --> 00:09:06.114
if you're not respecting your mother,

00:09:06.114 --> 00:09:08.868
your father, your uncles, your aunties

00:09:08.868 --> 00:09:11.509
half of them raised by the grandmother

00:09:11.509 --> 00:09:14.839
who's too old to actually
really do anything

00:09:14.839 --> 00:09:17.723
or put any real discipline down,

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:21.030
I'm just on this trip because
I'm a grandparent today too.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:23.520
My grandson really can't
do too much wrong, anyway.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.980
And I tell his mama, don't hit that boy,

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:26.820
you know what I'm saying?

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:30.029
But if they ain't got nobody to respect

00:09:30.029 --> 00:09:33.790
or nobody to look to for no
guidance on what it should be,

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:36.640
what do you think is going to happen?

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:39.540
If they run around, if
mom's taking the food stamps

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:41.230
and smoking them up with the dope, man

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.680
there ain't no food in the house.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.220
How was he going to respect her?

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.740
Now, if he don't respect his mama,

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.943
the fuck you think he gonna respect you?

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.420
So it all starts back.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.309
I mean it begins with drugs
and ends with drugs, man.

00:09:54.309 --> 00:09:56.147
- [Mark] In the families?

00:09:57.112 --> 00:10:00.076
- I mean, I don't want to go too far,

00:10:00.076 --> 00:10:02.526
but for the most part I
think they knew that too.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:04.763
It's fucked up.

00:10:04.763 --> 00:10:08.290
But I mean now it's a lot better

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.170
that this generation that's coming up now,

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.430
like they say in the Bible,

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:15.440
there's going to be wiser, but weaker.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:16.480
They smart as hell.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:17.810
Know how to use phones

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:20.060
and computers at one and two years old.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:23.550
A lot of them don't
believe in God, you know.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:26.708
Don't make sense their
computer and all that

00:10:26.708 --> 00:10:30.690
but it's not as much crack.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.500
And the parents are more at home now.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.050
So I don't think the next
generation is going to be as bad

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:38.170
as these.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.380
Because these kids, they
didn't have nothing,

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:42.670
they didn't have to respect nothing.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:45.090
So what do you expect them
to come out and respect

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:45.970
on the streets?

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:48.110
If you don't have to respect your mama,

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:50.060
see, I had to respect my mother.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:52.577
If I disrespect my mother,
I have about four uncles,

00:10:52.577 --> 00:10:55.220
they might not all come the same day,

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.510
but they coming to get that ass.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.770
Pops didn't stay at the house,

00:10:58.770 --> 00:10:59.605
he's coming to get that ass.

00:10:59.605 --> 00:11:02.643
And mom's going to get that ass.

00:11:03.874 --> 00:11:05.220
So I got about seven,
eight whoopers coming

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.270
for disrespecting my mom.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.240
These kids, they slapping their mamas

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:10.680
and calling them bitches.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.703
So if they going to do that
to the person that raised him

00:11:12.703 --> 00:11:17.320
what do you think he
cared about anything else?

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.390
So, you know, it's got to start over.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.860
We got to start all over
from the fabric, man.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.229
But that's my take home.

00:11:23.229 --> 00:11:24.600
That's a wrap.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:25.610
- [Mark] Thank you so
much for talking to me

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.020
